{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"attack-epidermoid-ekaltadeta","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nADR 0101 and the author-facing plan guide make `[non-codebase]` canonical while retaining `[operator-attested]` only as an undocumented compatibility alias. Closed migration story `unbeatable-unlit-gadwall` updated other user-visible remediation strings, but `operator_evidence_issues` still tells plan authors to add the legacy tag. Review result `a64d1c8b-0ed6-445c-ae31-f20f4a97312d` on `synonymous-senatorial-cuscus` reproduced the stale advice and caused an author to write both tags.\n\n## Approach\nChange only user-facing P6 coaching to prescribe `[non-codebase]`. Preserve the dual-token matcher and internal historical Python identifiers required for compatibility by ADR 0101. Add a regression assertion on the emitted coaching, then sweep active author-facing plan-review strings for the same stale prescription.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py` — replace the stale emitted remediation and align its author-facing docstrings/comments.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_advisory.py` — align the adjacent author-facing comment if retained.\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_portability.py` — assert coaching asks for the canonical tag and does not prescribe the legacy alias.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_portability.py` proves an untagged live outcome is coached to use `[non-codebase]`.\n- Compatibility edge: focused matcher tests continue proving both exact spellings parse, while malformed near-misses do not.\n- Sweep: `rg -n \"prefix.*operator-attested|not tagged \\[operator-attested\\]\" src/rebar/llm/plan_review` returns no active author-facing prescription.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] P6 feedback for an untagged outside-world criterion explicitly asks for `[non-codebase]`; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_portability.py`.\n- [ ] The compatibility matcher still accepts existing `[operator-attested]` tickets; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_non_codebase_tag.py`.\n- [ ] Active plan-review coaching contains no instruction to author new `[operator-attested]` tags; checked by the scoped `rg` sweep.","id":"2ebc-d3bd-9e50-4c2c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["plan-review","regression","documentation"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"P6 plan-review coaching emits legacy [operator-attested] tag"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787776217015778001,"uuid":"97d2337f-ff48-43a3-a0bf-58bbf0fb86fe"}